{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>First reading</b><br>לסוסתי (to my mare). The extra yud is like מלאתי משפט [I filled with justice], [אוהבתי לדוש (my beloved to thresh)]." "דמיתיך (I likened you). I compared you, like ואל מי תדמיון אל (and to whom would you liken El)." "<b>Second reading</b><br>לסוסתי ברכבי פרעה (to my mare in Pharaoh's chariot). For it is wood or iron. דמיתיך — this is a matter of the generation." "<b>Third reading</b><br>And when she repented, the Shekhinah said: לסוסתי [ברכבי פרעה] (to my mare in Pharaoh's chariot), דמיתיך — Congregation of Israel, for you bore the yoke of commandments and did not turn aside from the way; therefore I will give [your wage] and adorn you, and silver and gold you will bring out [with you] from Egypt."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "Bracketed Hebrew words inserted in brackets reflect likely abbreviations or variant readings in the manuscripts; translated as they appear in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:48.950298786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}